# A known_hosts entry that doesn't match the server's actual host key must be a hard
# error (the CheckResult::Mismatch branch in remote.rs's run_remote()) -- never silently
# connect anyway. See tests/system.rs's test_remote_ssh, which points
# CRUSH_TEST_SSH_HOSTS at a copy of the real known_hosts line with a few of the key's
# base64 characters corrupted, and checks (since a bare failing statement aborts the
# rest of the script -- there's deliberately no `echo` marker after this line to prove
# it) that stderr actually names a mismatch, not some other, coincidental failure.
remote:exec {(1 + 1)} "127.0.0.1:2849" username="crushtest" password="crushtest-password" host_file=$(crush:env["CRUSH_TEST_SSH_HOSTS"])
